{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-borromean-baryon","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:borromean-baryon","kind":"definition","title":"Borromean baryon","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hadron","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-pairwise-interaction-decomposition"],"tags":["borromean","baryon","unknot","color-confinement","link"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Braiding.BorromeanBaryon","text":"borromean-baryon.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/borromean-baryon.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:borromean-baryon\"></a><p>A <strong>Borromean baryon</strong> is a hadron whose three constituents are unknots <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K_{0_1}</code> joined by the Borromean link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}_3</code> and bound by the Hopf link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_H</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  B = \n  \\mathcal{B}_3(K_{0_1}, K_{0_1}, K_{0_1})\n   \\oplus  \\mathcal{L}_H</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/borromean-baryon.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"9.5.1"}
